WEBVTT

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.920
<i>All right, let's do this!</i>

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:38.150
Okay.  Please start your engines.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.640
Basic run, day 2.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:49.770
Please get the start right today, Capeta.

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:50.770
It'll be okay.

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:54.660
He's not going to lose to Shiba or that stuck-up girl.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:00.420
First, shift up.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:02.830
Rev limit 5000 rpm.

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:04.170
You get 15 minutes each.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:06.460
Listen.  Just relax.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:07.520
<b>Yes.</b>

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.400
Okay.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.170
<i>I'll be fine.</i>

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.060
<i>Just do as I did in the image training.</i>

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.120
<i>Set to first gear.</i>

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.770
<i>Pump the accel...</i>

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:22.230
<i>and the clutch...</i>

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:26.590
All right!  He got the start right!

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:30.950
Amazing!  He can start off now!

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.410
Way to go, Capeta!

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.580
Whoa!  Everyone went out on the first try!

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.230
Even the 5th car that failed yesterday!

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.210
<b>Attack, Taira.</b>

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:55.720
<b>Rev limit is 5000.</b>

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:56.640
<b>Okay.</b>

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:16.200
Incredible, Capeta!

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:50.730
<i>Everyone's sure learned quickly since yesterday.</i>

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:53.110
<i>These guys are amazing.</i>

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:56.810
Next, shift up plus full braking.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:58.950
Rev limit 6000 rpm.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.160
<i>Full braking at the straight end...</i>

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:10.580
<i>Listen up.</i>

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.720
<i>The difference from a kart is that there are also brakes in the front.</i>

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:19.180
<i>So if you brake hard while you're still going at a high speed like in a kart, the front will lock up.</i>

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:27.850
<i>First, gradually shift the weight toward the front and...</i>

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.110
<i>full braking!</i>

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:39.450
<i>Monami was right.</i>

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:41.970
<i>The basics of driving one of these aren't any different from a kart.</i>

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:45.960
<i>It's just loud, has a lid, and is a little faster, right?</i>

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:50.920
<i>As you said, formula cars aren't that different from karts.</i>

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:53.380
<i>But it might be more fun than karts.</i>

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:26.700
<b>Next, shift up plus heel-and-toe plus cornering!</b>

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:31.240
<b>Make sure to keep in mind what was taught in the lesson.</b>

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:35.420
<b>Each car, make sure to keep a distance from each other and drive safely.</b>

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:24.800
<b>Taira.</b>

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:26.220
<b>That wasn't bad.</b>

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:29.120
<i>He's not bad at driving.</i>

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:55.020
<i>They're amazing.</i>

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:57.040
<i>Racing drivers are amazing!</i>

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:02.660
<i>It didn't matter that he had no experience changing gears,</i>

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:06.350
<i>or that it was his first time in a formula machine.</i>

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:14.980
<i>Surely their problems and challenges don't come from there.</i>

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:19.550
<i>They must lie elsewhere.</i>

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:26.820
<i>It must be something, somewhere we can't possibly understand.</i>

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:29.450
<i>Damn.</i>

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:31.870
<i>Racing sure is great!</i>

00:08:37.670 --> 00:08:39.000
<i>I'll do it.</i>

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:41.210
<i>I may just be borrowing this...</i>

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:42.470
<i>but right now, it's mine!</i>

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:50.670
<i>I'll be the driver of this machine!</i>

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:04.150
Capeta sure is lucky.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:08.980
He's probably looking at the data logs and attending a lecture right now.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:11.620
I wish I could listen, too.

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:13.130
It can't be helped.

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:16.620
Besides, what's the point in staying in a dormitory with your parents around?

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:18.830
That's right.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:22.550
But Nobu-kun, you sure are optimistic.

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.270
Really?

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:25.830
Yeah, yeah.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:28.360
Yeah.

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:30.510
You're always studying and I'm impressed.

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:34.190
It's not that big a deal...

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:37.020
Okay.  Let's do it later.

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:40.550
We'll do it later.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:44.100
In any case, Monami-chan sure is late.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:46.530
Maybe she overcooked herself.

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:49.220
Maybe I should go check up on her.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:51.490
You shouldn't.

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:54.450
You'll be dead if you get caught.

00:09:54.850 --> 00:09:56.750
I was just kidding!

00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:58.760
I don't want to die yet.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:18.630
All right!

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:22.770
There!

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:28.830
Who was that?

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:40.070
This towel...

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:45.020
That bastard!

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:49.970
Hey, there's something I've been meaning to ask.

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:57.160
If Capeta passes the audition, he'll join a works team and compete in FSte races, right?

00:10:57.810 --> 00:11:01.980
Team Capeta will break up, but are you okay with that, Nobu-kun?

00:11:04.130 --> 00:11:09.860
Well, to be honest, I would have liked to race as Team Capeta a little more...

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:16.930
But really, we've come so far that we can't be saying that anymore.

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:20.800
That's why I went to the FSRS office personally.

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:23.460
And besides, if you think about it,

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:26.850
even if Capeta works with another team,

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:29.300
there will be a lot of things I can do.

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:33.270
There's something I need to think about.

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:35.720
Nobu-kun...  Is that...?

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:36.830
Yeah.  Something.

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:38.880
What do you mean, something?!

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:44.950
What's this?

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:45.980
My towel.

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:47.820
I see...

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:49.920
So it was you!

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:50.650
Ow!

00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:51.740
What's that for?!

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:54.200
Taira...

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:57.580
you're braking too softly on the first corner.

00:11:57.580 --> 00:11:58.500
Okay.

00:11:58.500 --> 00:11:59.520
Now look.

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:02.150
I'll overlap Ishihara's data over yours.

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:04.780
Here.

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:08.440
As pacesetter, Ishihara is stepping this hard.

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:10.970
And compared to that, you're only stepping this much.

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:18.510
So, compared to Ishihara, your weight at the front is less, and your steering is weaker.

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:21.250
That's why you can't do sharp turns.

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:21.930
Okay.

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:26.440
Therefore, in order to make a sharp turn,
 what would you need to do?

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:32.400
As you can see, Ishihara is delaying his braking up to the straight end here.

00:12:33.050 --> 00:12:36.370
Up to 10 meters further in.

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:41.610
If you brake at the position you did,
you'll have some braking time left over...

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:44.650
so you'd have to release the brake pedal and step on it again.

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:47.830
Therefore you're losing that weight you gained at the front.

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:54.270
So, if you delay your timing on the brake longer,

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:57.600
not only would you have more time to accelerate...

00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:00.390
but you could also step on the brake harder.

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:04.560
You'll turn faster, so you'll be able to accelerate faster as well.

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:07.080
It's the best rotation.

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:08.100
I understand.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:10.100
Now, as for the second corner...

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:14.400
<i>Wow, with so many data logs, I'll know everything!</i>

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:16.370
<i>I didn't know there was such a thing!</i>

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:21.290
<i>I'll know what to do to improve, so at this rate I'll get much better!</i>

00:13:29.010 --> 00:13:30.030
How is it this year?

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:31.670
Anyone who stands out?

00:13:32.650 --> 00:13:35.010
It's not too bad, but still...

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:37.590
There's no one like Minamoto this year.

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:39.810
Oh.  Naomi, huh?

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:44.640
Last year he broke all the times set by our pacesetter Ishihara on the last day.

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:48.810
And what do you have to say to that, regular driver Ishihara-kun?

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:51.300
Not much point in being the pacesetter, is there?

00:13:51.950 --> 00:13:52.780
I'm sorry.

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:55.740
Well, Minamoto last year was an exception.

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:57.470
Don't get pulled in by it.

00:13:57.470 --> 00:13:59.830
Drivers like him only come around
 once every ten or twenty years anyway.

00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:03.430
Everyone, please reset your minds and proceed with the evaluations.

00:14:03.430 --> 00:14:05.250
We know, Makoto-san.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:19.870
Image training, huh?

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:22.810
You sure are serious, Taira.

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:27.360
Shinkawa-san told me I should do at least 100 laps before sleeping.

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:29.350
A-Aren't you going to do it, Shiba-kun?

00:14:29.350 --> 00:14:31.130
Just Ryou is fine.

00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:32.770
Otherwise it's just creepy. {M: as in being called formally}

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:35.880
Are you really going to do 100 laps?

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:41.740
I keep messing up somewhere along the line,
 so I have to start over again...

00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:44.580
So I don't get far.

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:46.490
What should I do?!

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:48.790
I won't be able to sleep at this rate!

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:53.060
I lose my strength watching you.

00:14:56.820 --> 00:15:00.180
To think that you were that driver then.

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:06.640
Seriously?!

00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:10.320
Shiba seems to be the best so far this year.

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:13.510
Shiba, as in the guy who attached a letter with his application?

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:14.410
Yeah.

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:17.980
The one who wrote, "I'll make it up to the F1 no matter what, so pleased to be working with you."

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:19.880
He's fast.

00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:21.700
And his line is the best so far.

00:15:21.700 --> 00:15:23.700
What do you think, Shinkawa-san?

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:24.620
Me?

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:29.470
I have this feeling that there will be one more who will surprise us.

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:30.540
Who is it?

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:32.630
You'll know soon enough.

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:35.740
Hey.

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:36.820
Was that on purpose?

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:38.430
Huh?  What do you mean?

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:40.590
That last corner at Haruna...

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:44.080
where you collided with that lapped driver and turned, that's what.

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:53.400
Were you planning on that when you plunged in?

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:57.170
Hm... well...

00:15:57.170 --> 00:15:58.390
How was it...

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:00.010
Don't act stupid.

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:05.010
If you did it on purpose, you would have gotten a penalty for dangerous driving...

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:07.620
but no one would have blamed you
 since you had broken ribs.

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:09.870
It was all calculated, huh?

00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:11.330
It wasn't!

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:16.090
We had to win that race no matter what.

00:16:16.090 --> 00:16:20.670
And maybe I did think about it somewhere in my head.

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:23.340
But I really don't remember any of it!

00:16:25.280 --> 00:16:27.760
My body just did it!

00:16:28.470 --> 00:16:29.230
What?!

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:30.770
You want to blame me?!

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:34.730
What are you getting all worked up for?

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:38.960
If I was in your position,
 I would've done the same thing.

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:41.690
So I won't blame you.

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:45.700
I just wanted to ask.

00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:47.890
See ya.

00:16:52.600 --> 00:16:53.620
Oh yeah.

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:56.080
About the image training.

00:16:56.530 --> 00:17:00.050
I just got 30.89 seconds.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:03.030
I'll beat you by a wide margin this time.

00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:06.060
What?!

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:09.360
How can you know the time from an image training?!

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:11.970
And in the 30-second range?!

00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:14.760
That's just a bluff!

00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:16.980
Just concentrate!

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:30.980
Hey, Taira.

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:33.480
Are you sure she's not your girlfriend?

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:34.870
Of course.

00:17:35.270 --> 00:17:36.680
Come on.  Please!

00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:38.790
Tell me her number, please!

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:40.840
It's okay if she's not your girlfriend, right?

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:42.400
That's...

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:44.090
What.  You're holding it back after all.

00:17:44.090 --> 00:17:45.800
She is your girlfriend.

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:47.240
That's not it.

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:49.520
My friend has a crush on her.

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:53.030
And Monami gets all scary if I give anyone her number.

00:17:53.030 --> 00:17:54.950
You're being suspicious.

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:56.640
Hey, you two!

00:17:57.710 --> 00:17:59.520
Stop it already.

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:00.990
That's right.

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:03.440
You guys aren't tense enough!

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:05.710
The mock race is today!

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:13.300
That's why I want to get this off my mind and concentrate!

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:13.950
Really.

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:19.130
It's just not right bringing a girl here anyway.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.060
What's the big deal?!

00:18:21.060 --> 00:18:22.380
What are you getting jealous for?!

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:24.430
I'm not jealous!

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:28.310
<i>Damn... I can't concentrate...</i>

00:18:28.310 --> 00:18:30.910
<i>And just when I finally got it right in the image training.</i>

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:36.100
What's the matter, Isa-kun?  You're getting too nervous.

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:37.600
Y-Yes.

00:18:37.600 --> 00:18:41.090
You won't be able to drive your best if you don't relax, okay?

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:41.860
Yes.

00:19:00.010 --> 00:19:04.230
<i>For some of you, this may be your last day driving in the FSte today.</i>

00:19:04.230 --> 00:19:06.440
<i>You have to do your best in this mock race.</i>

00:19:06.440 --> 00:19:08.500
<i>To be honest, the qualifier is everything.</i>

00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:10.970
<i>Drive as if your life depended on it.</i>

00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:19.600
This free run is your last chance to practice before the qualifier.

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:20.800
Now listen up!

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:25.070
Drive as if you intend on beating Ishihara, our pacesetter's time!

00:19:25.070 --> 00:19:27.530
<i>That Makoto-san...</i>

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:44.710
Capeta!

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:15.610
<b>Ishihara, 31.14 seconds!</b>

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:26.010
<b>Taira, 31.83 seconds!</b>

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:33.000
<b>Shiba, 31.27 seconds!</b>

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:34.510
<b>Not bad, Shiba!</b>

00:20:34.510 --> 00:20:37.280
<b>He's shaved 0.6 seconds off his best time yesterday!</b>

00:20:37.280 --> 00:20:39.600
All right!

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:46.230
<b>Hata, 31.61 seconds!</b>

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:50.940
Daiki, 31.69 seconds!

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:55.870
Isa, 32.11 seconds!

00:20:56.650 --> 00:20:59.780
<b>Whoa!  Taira, 31.51 seconds!</b>

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:01.360
<b>Followed by Shiba...</b>

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:04.550
<b>Wow, 31 seconds flat!</b>

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:09.340
<i>Damn it!  I won't lose!</i>

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:15.570
<i>I won't lose!!</i>

00:22:51.020 --> 00:22:53.520
Capeta, you're just too incredible!

00:22:54.070 --> 00:22:57.890
To think that in two days, you've caught up with those who have already practiced!{alt: In two days, you've caught up with those who have already practiced!}

00:22:58.910 --> 00:22:59.610
Capeta...!

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:01.530
Next time, on Capeta.

00:23:01.530 --> 00:23:03.260
Blind Corner!

00:23:03.260 --> 00:23:04.990
Open up the future!
